 "strings": {
  "The Lone Swordsmen": "",
  "Scion of the Hozoin Spear": "",
  "The Ever-Victorious Fighter": "",
  "A Weapon Merchant Hungry for Vengeance": "",
  "The Faithful Kodachi Wielder": "",
  "Passionate Swordsman from Nobility": "",
  "Eye for an Iai": "",
  "Assassination Specialist": "",
  "The Ultimate Masseuse": "",
  "One Who Has Perfected Judo": "",
  "The Farmer Who Would Cross the Sea": "",
  "Shinobi Chief with a Pure Heart": "",
  "Gold-Armored Warrior, Not Yet Armored": "",
  "A Man of Bearlike Integrity": "",
  "The Awakened Patrolman": "",
  "The Outcast Monk of Despair": "",
  "Aficionado of Beautiful Swords": "",
  "Farmer with a Bloody Hoe": "",
  "Kabuki Actor with Crimson Makeup": "",
  "Late-Blooming Swordsman": "",
  "A Man More Feared Than Demons": "",
  "Won the Match": "",
  "With the belief that soft and fair goes far, he has devoted himself to judo. Many have tried to throw him, but all were taken down. As people seeking glory began to ambush him, he took to walking through town in a constant parry stance. However, local women complained that this was an obscene way to position his hands. The complaint deeply wounded him, driving him to Mukurogai.": "",
  "Hailing from a nice household, he enjoyed a stable life but grew pudgy. He showed unexpected talent for swordsmanship when he began practicing it for exercise, and decided to enter the arena. His skills are improving, but his belly fat has been very stubborn.": "",
  "He yearns for the golden armor he once heard about in a children's story. To pursue this dream, he entered the arena for the prize money. He also works as a clerk at an udon shop in Rakunai and does day-to-day labor. He has yet to encase himself in golden armor and lives a simple life to save as much as he can.": "",
  "Previously worked as a gatekeeper for a wealthy man. His defense against intruders was so well-known, a thief avoided the gate and entered from the backyard. This worked, and the wealthy man had his entire fortune stolen. When the magistrate came to investigate, the gatekeeper took him for an intruder and prevented his entrance. Now out of a job, he supports himself through the arena.": "",
  "He used to be a town magistrate, but his kind expression demanded no authority. He tried to become scarier but overdid it and was fired from his position. Put on a mask and be feared, take it off and nobody takes you seriously. Ruefully bitter at this unfair world, he took up the mace and fights in the arena.": "",
  "A sumo whose fellow wrestler was murdered by the Shinsengumi. To avenge his colleague's death, he abandoned the rank of Ozeki and keeps watch over the arena to see if any Shinsengumi enter. He is a kind man, but becomes reckless and unstoppable in a fight.": "",
  "When he shot a pistol that he happened to pick up from the riverbed, he struck a pot on the other side of the water. He's been called a master gunman ever since. He trains to be worthy of the title and competes in the arena to help offset the cost of bullets. There's been no sign that he could hit that pot again.": "",
  "The distant relative of a feudal lord, he was born into a venerable samurai family. Left home after clashing with his father, and developed a strong loyalty to the Shogun. He came to Kyo to defeat the loyalists, but found himself disheartened by their numbers and decided to only fight shishi that enter the arena.": "",
  "He was once inspired to eschew justice for villainy. Looking down upon those living quiet lives, he sought to drive them to despair through theft and violence. However, when his sole relative—his mother—became sick, he renounced his ways. Knowing only sin, he fights in the arena to pay for her care.": "",
  "Whenever he holds his sword with both hands, he is troubled by a mysterious medical condition which causes his left hand to itch unbearably. For this reason, he has devoted himself to the art of quick-draw: iaijutsu, which only requires his right hand to unsheathe his blade and attack. His skills are peerless—he can cut a large tree down to a stump. When necessary, he sometimes holds his sword with both hands, if he can stand the itch.": "",
  "An official who made a name for himself in a town not far from Kyo. Secretly an unparalleled gun nut, in his home he would collect money through virtuous words, then use the funds to modify his firearms. He is a crazed man who heard rumors of the arena and came to test his weaponry.": "",
  "The representative of the Touken Clan, a group which gathers in Fushimi to collect swords. Has extensive knowledge of blades and can't resist rare katanas. Of course, he also practices his swordsmanship without fail, and has enough skill to defeat any ordinary samurai. He heard rumors of rare weapons at the arena and came to see for himself.": "",
  "The leader of the Chivalrous Shinobi, who operate out of Fushimi. They steal money from the wicked and use it to help orphans and the poor. Their ways brought them popularity among the city of Kyo. He has entered the arena in order to earn money to help his sick sister, Oharu.": "",
  "He once joined the sword-collecting Touken Clan. Believing enchanted swords were evil, he couldn't abide their decision to start collecting cursed blades and left. However, after he joined the arena, his beliefs began to change. He now realizes that enchanted swords are still swords, and worthy of love.": "",
  "Gun-toting ninja formerly of the Chivalrous Shinobi. A virtuous man who fights for the commonfolk, he left the group when its leader abandoned their chivalrous ideals. As his former comrades try to kill him, he hides himself in Mukurogai and trains in order to build the Chivalrous Shinobi anew.": "",
  "The master of the Komaki Dojo, who teaches the ancient Komaki style. He does not believe in carrying weapons, and has always fought unarmed. Even in his old age, his skills have not waned. He is a well-known sensei to those who fight barehanded.": "",
  "A farmer famous in his hometown for producing oddly delicious vegetables. Rumors abound that he uses some secret kind of fertilizer. Of course, his village was also the site of a series of unsolved murders... Could it be? Fleeing suspicion, he absconded from his home and now this crazed, homicidal farmer fights in the arena.": "",
  "The young successor of the Hozoin spear technique, passed down from the Azuchi-Momoyama period. His spear skills are said to be on par with the style's founder, Inei. However, in this time of unrest, he fears his style may die out were it restricted to a dojo, and carries it on through the arena instead.": "",
  "A self-proclaimed kabuki actor with no stage name. He has the makeup, but his true identity is a wanted man who has beaten dozens of samurai to death with his bare hands. As of now, he resides in Kyo—where being in an actor's getup garners no extra attention—and lives off the earnings from the arena.": "",
  "He lost his parents when a bear attacked his village. However, he was then taken in by the bear, and was raised with the animal's family in the wild. Once his grizzly foster passed away, he attempted to reenter society. Finding no place for himself, he earns his way through the arena, where he mauls his opponents with his bearlike body—and a mace.": "",
  "To further his skills, he traveled Japan for years, challenging dojos with only spear in hand. When he finally mastered the weapon, he triumphantly returned to Kyo. However, the city had become turbulent, and carrying a spear meant one could be attacked at any moment. A timid man at heart, he decided to start going to the arena in secret.": "",
  "He had been training at a temple since he was a child, but fell for a beautiful woman at first sight one day. As the temple's strict dogma would not allow their love, the man left in pursuit of her. But, the woman he loved would lose her life at the hands of a street killer. Plunged into the depths of despair, he entered the arena where killers gather to find the culprit.": "",
  "A law enforcement official who patrolled the city with his beloved jitte. He heard that a fugitive he was chasing was seen in the arena and decided to enter. Though he caught his man, he found pleasure in beating people senseless in this new lawless environment and has kept coming back.": "",
  "Wanting to be famous, he joined the Jozo Tengu because of their notorious reputation. Finding out that they were a group of evildoers who would steal and use violence, he fled after half a day. However, he couldn't give up on his dream, and entered the arena. He doesn't take off the tengu mask, since he thinks it's cool.": "",
  "The heir to a family of spear users, he was trained in using one since birth, yet always yearned to study swordsmanship. One day he went behind his father's back to a dojo to train with swordsmen, but was able to defeat every student and the master with his spear. \"Maybe spears are pretty good after all,\" he thought, and entered the arena to further hone his skills.": "",
  "Ran a family carpentry business in Edo. He would miss the nails with his hammer often and was so hurt by the laughter of his apprentices that he came to Kyo. While he's acquired a gigantic hammer that easily hits its mark, he is now troubled by the fact that its impact shatters the lumber.": "",
  "He ran a shiatsu massage place, but through his work gained so much strength in his fingers that he could break roof tiles with just the press of his thumbs. Naturally, his shiatsu became too strong, with customers suffering broken bones and torn ligaments. He entered the arena to keep his business afloat.": "",
  "An arms dealer who does business in Rakugai. As he commands many of the local ronin, he has a very wide information network. While he was searching for the most effective way to use firearms, he developed first-class shooting skills before he knew it.": "",
  "A swordsman who pursues beauty in combat. He's earned some local fame through his dojo in Rakunai. Beneath his humble demeanor, he is the heir to the noble Ayanokoji family. He hones his skills within the arena, so as to never forsake the beauty of swordplay.": "",
  "A master of his own sword style—Goyo style, which specializes in various stances. He is skilled, but has trouble gaining students as his eyes are too piercing. In the arena, he hides under a straw hat, and recruits opponents he defeats.": "",
  "The leader of an armed gang, the Jozo Tengu. His true face is a mystery, even to his own men. To atone for the troubles he's caused, he participates in the arena and donates his winnings to charity.": "",
  "Born into a noble family, he lived a comfortable life, but came to feel a strong sense of duty during this time of unrest. Leaving home with only his sword, he wandered his way into Mukurogai, where he learned of the arena. It was there, among the heated battles, that he felt the changing of the age. He now fights to keep from being left behind.": "",
  "In the long history of the arena, this man holds the highest winning streak. He entered as an amateur originally, but suffered an overwhelming defeat in his first match. From there, his immense desire for revenge drove him to train. He competes daily, but the man who gave him his only loss has never reappeared.": "",
  "He started an organization called the Shokko School, where he preached that eating is the highest form of happiness. Sadly, no one has enrolled. To show the world the greatness of his teachings, he takes on the arena with powerful moves that utilize his size. The box he carries on his back is filled to the brim with freshly cooked rice.": "",
  "When the Black Ships arrived, he was present at Uraga. Wanting to travel overseas, he stowed away on one of them. However, he was discovered by the crew, and thrown overboard partway through the journey. He swam back to Japan, gripping the gun he stole from the ship. He competes in the arena to pay for a true trip abroad.": "",
